{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02449",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.68,
      "end_seconds": 8.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.76,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.38,
      "end_seconds": 14.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Perfect, thanks. Hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.04,
      "end_seconds": 19.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got no symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 21.0,
      "end_seconds": 30.66,
      "duration_seconds": 9.66,
      "text": "here are the numbers, doctor temperature 37.0, pulse is 85 beats a minute, saturation 99 percent, respiratory rate 15, pressure 119 over 70."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.56,
      "end_seconds": 37.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Good, thank you. How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.92,
      "end_seconds": 39.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "About... well, four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.1,
      "end_seconds": 44.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "right, right. Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.8,
      "end_seconds": 51.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "I'd call it severe"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.48,
      "end_seconds": 55.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.36,
      "end_seconds": 78.68,
      "duration_seconds": 21.32,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a high blood sugar on a routine test as well. As for high blood sugar on a routine test, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.69,
      "end_seconds": 95.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Okay, any blurred vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.39,
      "end_seconds": 100.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "not that I've noticed, no blurred vision"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.76,
      "end_seconds": 106.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "a few quick ones: weight loss, frequent urination or thirst?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.15,
      "end_seconds": 111.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "I haven't had weight loss, frequent urination or thirst, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.73,
      "end_seconds": 118.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "So, has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.18,
      "end_seconds": 121.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.58,
      "end_seconds": 126.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.52,
      "end_seconds": 130.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.91,
      "end_seconds": 133.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.29,
      "end_seconds": 138.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "I've had gout for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.68,
      "end_seconds": 144.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.84,
      "end_seconds": 156.67,
      "duration_seconds": 10.83,
      "text": "I'm on allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day for the gout. I used to take febuxostat, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.05,
      "end_seconds": 165.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.26,
      "end_seconds": 172.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Hmm, yes, nickel, it gives me a rash on my skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.08,
      "end_seconds": 192.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "how active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.39,
      "end_seconds": 198.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.93,
      "end_seconds": 203.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Alright, what do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.32,
      "end_seconds": 208.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.93,
      "end_seconds": 211.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.35,
      "end_seconds": 216.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.33,
      "end_seconds": 222.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.81,
      "end_seconds": 225.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.49,
      "end_seconds": 229.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.42,
      "end_seconds": 251.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "your blood pressure and heart rate are normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.39,
      "end_seconds": 261.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.35,
      "text": "you can relax now taking everything into account, I think we're dealing with prediabetes at this stage"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.81,
      "end_seconds": 264.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.49,
      "end_seconds": 276.02,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the the moment I'd say it's prediabetes, and we'll know more once the a repeat HbA1c is back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.07,
      "end_seconds": 297.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "I think a repeat HbA1c makes sense here, for prediabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.73,
      "end_seconds": 302.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Oh, that's fine with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.34,
      "end_seconds": 315.3,
      "duration_seconds": 11.96,
      "text": "Walk thirty minutes daily, cut sugary drinks and aim to lose five percent of your weight. I'm gonna send a referral to the diabetes prevention programme."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.47,
      "end_seconds": 323.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.34,
      "end_seconds": 338.18,
      "duration_seconds": 12.84,
      "text": "Please don't wait if the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently. We'll catch up in six months. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.96,
      "end_seconds": 340.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}